# 15. FINANCIAL DATA HANDLING

This application handles financial transactions.

Follow these rules strictly.

## Currency

- Display currency in INR.
- Use the Indian number format.
- Display values with two decimal places where appropriate.
- Inspect whether the backend returns amounts in paise or rupees.
- If the backend stores amounts in paise, convert them for display only.
- Never modify the original API amount unexpectedly.

Use a shared currency formatting utility.

## Transaction forms

Deposit:

- Select an eligible account.
- Enter amount.
- Enter description/reference if supported.
- Confirm transaction.

Withdrawal:

- Select an eligible account.
- Enter amount.
- Enter description/reference if supported.
- Confirm transaction.

Transfer:

- Select source account.
- Select permitted destination account.
- Enter amount.
- Enter description/reference if supported.
- Confirm transaction.

Use the actual backend validation rules.

Show clear success and failure messages.

Prevent accidental duplicate submissions while a transaction is processing.

Do not create fake transaction success responses.

## Amount precision

Never use floating-point arithmetic to calculate financial balances.

Do not calculate or modify authoritative balances in the frontend.

The backend is the source of truth for balances and transaction results.

Do not convert amounts between rupees and paise without verifying the backend contract.

